hadiths[11]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2176","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The good dreams of a righteous person are one part out of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"2177","‘Sayyiduna Abu Sa‘id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) heard from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that’ the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “When any one of you sees a dream that he finds good, then it is from Allah. He should thank Allah for it and relate it (to his friends). And if he sees other than that, a dream that seems bad, then it is from Satan. He should seek refuge with Allah from its evil and not mention it to anyone, for then it will not harm him.”"
"2178","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say, ""Nothing of prophethood remains except glad tidings (mubashshirat)."" The companions asked, ""What are glad tidings?"" He (peace be upon him) said, ""Good dreams."" (Mubashshirat means glad tidings and good news.)"
"2179","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me in a dream will soon see me while awake, and Satan cannot take my form."
"2180","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Whoever sees me (in a dream), indeed he has seen me, for Satan cannot imitate my appearance."
"2181","`Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to visit Umm Haram bint Milhan (may Allah be pleased with her), and she was the wife of Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him). One day, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) went to her, and she served him food and began to look at his head as if searching for lice. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) fell asleep, and then when he woke up, he woke up smiling. Umm Haram said, ""O Messenger of Allah! What makes you smile?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Some people from my Ummah were shown to me, fighting in the way of Allah, riding on the sea (on ships), like kings on thrones or like kings sitting on their thrones."" This doubt is from the narrator Ishaq. Umm Haram (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""I said, O Messenger of Allah! Pray to Allah that He makes me among them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed for her, then rested his head and slept again. Then he woke up smiling. Umm Haram (may Allah be pleased with her) said, ""I said, O Messenger of Allah! (Now) what makes you smile?"" He said: ""Some people from my Ummah were presented before me, fighting in the way of Allah,"" as he had said the first time. She said, ""I said, Pray to Allah that He makes me among them."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""You will be among the first ones."" Thus, Umm Haram (may Allah be pleased with her) boarded a ship in the sea during the caliphate of Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Abu Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him), and when she came out of the sea, she fell from her riding animal and passed away."
"2182","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""When the Hour draws near, the dream of a believer will not be false (rather, it will be absolutely true), and the dream of a believer is one part out of forty-six parts of Prophethood, and whatever is from Prophethood can never be false."
"2183","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I saw (in a dream) as if a black woman with unkempt hair was coming out of Medina and settling at Mahya‘ah (i.e., Al-Juhfa)."" (The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said:) ""I interpreted that as the epidemic of Medina being transferred there."
"2184","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever describes a dream which he did not see (i.e., lies), he will be made to tie two grains of barley together on the Day of Resurrection, but he will not be able to do so. And whoever listens to the conversation of people who dislike him listening and move away from him, molten lead will be poured into his ears on the Day of Resurrection. And whoever makes a picture, he will be punished and will be asked to put a soul into it, but he will not be able to do so."
"2185","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""The greatest lie is that a person claims to have seen something with his eyes (i.e., a dream) which he has not seen."
"2186","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with both of them) narrates that` a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! I saw in a dream at night that there was a canopy (cloud) and from it ghee and honey were dripping, and people were collecting it, some more, some less. And I saw a rope extending from the sky to the earth, and I saw you (peace and blessings be upon him) holding it and ascending. Then after you, another person held it and he also ascended by it. Then another person held it and ascended, then after them another person held it, but the rope broke, and then it was joined again."" Sayyiduna Abu Bakr Siddiq (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""O Messenger of Allah! Allow me to interpret this dream."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Alright, interpret it."" He said, ""The canopy is Islam, and the ghee and honey dripping from it is the Noble Qur'an and its recitation, and those who collect it are those who acquire the Qur'an, some more, some less. And the rope extending from the sky to the earth is the truth which Allah Almighty has revealed to you. By holding it, Allah will raise you up, and after you, another person will hold it and ascend, and then another person will ascend, and then another person will hold it, but the rope will break. Then it will be joined again, and he will also ascend. O Messenger of Allah! May my parents be sacrificed for you, tell me, did I interpret correctly or did I make a mistake?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You have interpreted some correctly and made some mistakes."" He said, ""O Messenger of Allah! By Allah, tell me what mistake I made."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Do not swear."
